  "status": "Application Under Consideration",
  "description": "The proposal involves the conversion of an existing Class C3 residential dwelling into a Class C2 residential care facility. The use will provide specialist, supported accommodation for adults with mental health needs, delivered within a small-scale, domestic-style setting that replicates the character of a home environment while offering appropriate levels of professional support.\nThe residential care facility will be operated by Essex Homes Ltd, under the direction of an experienced mental health nurse with over 40 years of professional practice and registration with the RMC. The residential care facility is committed to delivering high-quality, person-centred support for residents in Walthamstow and the surrounding areas. Essex Homes Ltd will be registered with the Care Quality Commission (CQC) and will adhere to all regulatory standards to ensure excellent levels of care, safeguarding, and operational oversight.\nThe property is expected to accommodate six residents, supported at all times by two on-site staff, ensuring an appropriate level of supervision and personalised support. Staff will operate on a structured rota, as follows:\n\n08:45 – 15:00\n\n14:45 – 21:00\n\n08:45 – 08:45 (24-hour shift)\n\nThis proposed use will contribute positively to the borough’s provision of specialist accommodation by meeting an identified need for mental health support services. It will help foster a balanced, inclusive, and supportive community, while providing a stable environment for vulnerable adults who require ongoing care and supervision.",
